AnimY is a personal web application designed for tracking and searching anime titles. It provides a streamlined interface for fans to manage their favorites and discover new series using real-time data.

## Core Features

Anime Discovery: Search for a wide range of titles powered by the Jikan API.

Favorites Management: A dedicated system for users to track and manage their personal anime lists.

Dynamic UI: A responsive and user-centric design focused on providing an intuitive browsing experience.

## Tech Stack

Frontend: Built with React, utilizing functional components and hooks for state management.

Backend: Powered by Express.js to handle API routing and server-side logic.

Database: Leverages PostgreSQL (via Supabase) for reliable data storage and retrieval.

Data Source: Integrates the Jikan API for comprehensive and up-to-date anime metadata.

## Technical Highlights

Security: Implemented Supabase Row-Level Security (RLS) policies to ensure user data remains private and secure.

Modular Design: Utilizes a structured architectural approach to maintain clean code across both the React frontend and the Express backend.

## About the Developer

Developed by Vincent Yuan, a Computer Science student at Drexel University. This project showcases a full-stack integration of modern web technologies and a passion for the anime community.
